WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.877
5S sounds like a factory programme.

00:00:05.157 --> 00:00:08.650
But it starts at one workstation, and it starts with the furniture.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:15.378
Many 5S drives fail after a few weeks, because tools and parts still have no fixed place,

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:17.168
so clutter slowly returns.

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:22.040
5S means Sort, Set in order, Shine, Standardise and Sustain.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.741
Furniture supports the middle three: a fixed home for every item, surfaces that are easy to clean,

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:32.279
and identical stations that make the standard obvious.

00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:37.326
Sort and Sustain depend on people, but good furniture makes them far easier.

00:00:37.926 --> 00:00:44.161
Furnisys stations make this practical: pegboards and holders for tools, bin rails for parts,

00:00:44.161 --> 00:00:49.515
drawer partitions, and marker or tack boards for standard operating procedures.

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:53.864
A valve maker uses the marker board for batch data at each station.

00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:56.984
When every item has a home, 5S sticks.

00:00:57.264 --> 00:00:59.216
Which S does your team find hardest?

00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:03.919
Comment below, and next, see how to design motion waste out of a station.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:08.764
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

